      "content": "i see what u mean about the rigidity. could you take it a step further? \n\ni need you to really hammer home the technical specifics of why this sparsity approach is risky. if you could break it down into a few bulleted points—maybe one specifically on the math of the top-k selection and another on the empirical evidence being lacking—that would be great. \n\nagain, just be careful not to lose the actual technical reasoning in a sea of \"critical\" words. i just need the critique to feel heavy and authoritative, not like it's just repeating the same negative descriptors over and over. make it sound like a seasoned researcher who is genuinely concerned about the methodology.",
